    "whatItTellsYou": "A taller Shannon/Simpson bar means a more diverse community — richer and/or more even. Comparing bars ranks sites; a bar that is low despite many species collected signals dominance by one or two species (low evenness), while similar heights across sites suggest a treatment did not change diversity. Because the index collapses richness and evenness into one number, pair it with a rank-abundance plot to see which of the two is driving a difference.",
